From 629434517dfd62a3ed49ca912e29e53c58699812 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mrinohk <5554998+Mrinohk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:29:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 33/35] p60 exact: persistent MoE half, bit-identical to stock
 decode (v1)

GGML_CUDA_P60_MEGAX=1 (with GGML_CUDA_P60_EXACT=1): tagged generation
steps (1..6 tokens) run the MoE half of a layer as one cooperative
kernel (p60-mega-x.cu). Each warp emulates the stock kernel it
replaces: mul_mat_vec_q with 4 warps (partials of warps 1..3 added in
order, then the xor butterfly), mul_mat_vec_f with 8 warps,
rms_norm_f32<1024>, quantize_q8_1, topk_moe_cuda<256>,
moe_weighted_reduction_f32 and the fused add chain. vec_dot and float
expressions are the stock ones. GGML_CUDA_P60_MEGAX_DUMP=layer (99 =
all) writes intermediates for debugging.

Measured (greedy, 3 real harness prompts): logits bit-identical to
stock T=1 for T=1..6 over 160 rows; llama-server MTP + EXACT + MEGAX
token-identical to stock without speculation. Decode with MTP 79-92 ->
85-98 t/s. v1 has one warp per row and does not share weight loads
across tokens yet.

